  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Barkley Sound Zooplankton, 1991-present",
  "description": "Tombstone (length, weight, sex, maturity, stage, species) of zooplankton collected by Ron Tanasichuk in Barkley Sound from 1991 to the present. Dataset is used to describe variations in population biology of zooplankton.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Used continuously by custodian to learn about variations in population biology and productivity of key fish prey. Objective is to evaluate effect of changes in fish prey biology on population biology and productivity of fish populations.\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Data are in electronic format, well backed up and well documented. Risk of Loss: Low Impact Justification: Long-term time series of broad applicability. Impact of Loss: Medium",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23570060",
